.TH tix-ticket-setup 1  "setup " 
.SH NAME
tix\-ticket\-setup \- Create a new ticket workspace with worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix ticket setup\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> [\fIREPO_ALIASES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new ticket workspace with worktrees
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
The key recorded for the ticket, defaulting to the directory name. Path form only — a bare key already names itself
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-project\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The project to create the ticket in, created on first use. Inferred from the current directory when omitted; outside any project the ticket is loose. Key form only — a path already says where it goes
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Human\-readable description; feeds branch name derivation
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<REFISH>\fR
What each new branch is cut from: a branch name (local or origin\*(Aqs, whichever is ahead), or any ref, tag, or SHA. Defaults to each repository\*(Aqs own default branch on origin
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Include every registered repository
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
Where the ticket goes: a bare key (e.g. JIRA\-123) created under the tickets directory, or a path (anything containing a separator, or `.`/`..`) created at that location
.TP
[\fIREPO_ALIASES\fR]
Repositories to include (defaults to `[defaults].repositories`)
